# What the build does NOT need to see.
#
# Vercel uploads the working directory, and .gitignore is not reliably honoured —
# without this file the 750 MB of GHS-POP tiles and GeoNames dumps under data/ get
# sent to the build, which fails the upload outright. Everything the app needs was
# already distilled into src/scenes/ by scripts/build-region.py and committed.

# Source rasters and dumps. Distilled outputs are committed; these are not.
data/

# Build artefacts — Vercel builds from source.
.next/
out/
node_modules/

# Local-only, and never to leave this machine.
.local/
docs/references/
docs/programme-context.md

# The STL print tool. THIS IS THE GATE, and it is the only one.
#
# `output: 'export'` means there is no server and therefore no auth to hide an internal
# route behind. So the route is not hidden, it is ABSENT: the Vercel build never sees
# this directory, and the deployed export has no /print page and no chunk to read.
#
# It still works under `npm run dev` and in a locally built export — which is the
# exhibition laptop, the machine that will be driving the printer.
#
# Deleting this line publishes the tool. Nothing in the code would stop it, because an
# env flag that ships the page anyway is not a gate. See src/app/print/page.tsx.
src/app/print/

# Scratch
*.log
__pycache__/
*.pyc
